{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1692361792/16/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"41ace6b5\" lines=\"7-26\">\n<description>\nNormalize vertical two-color bars between paired marker columns around the marker rows.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- A row of red marker pixels sits directly above a row of gray marker pixels\n  in the same alternating columns.\n- The columns between adjacent markers contain vertical bars made from a\n  contiguous teal run above a contiguous blue run.\n\nRule\n- Keep the marker pixels and all non-bar background cells fixed.\n- Let h be the maximum teal-run height among the bar columns; paint teal in\n  every bar column for h rows ending at the red marker row.\n- In each bar column, move its blue run to start at the gray marker row and\n  fill all lower cells in that column with maroon.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker rows are a baseline: teal is normalized into a common upper\n  band, while each blue run keeps its own height below the baseline.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"20fb2937\" lines=\"63-77\">\n<description>\nReplace each marker below the separator with the mapped top legend square centered on that marker.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background surrounds a top legend, one solid non-background separator row, and a lower marker field.\n- The legend contains equal-size filled square sprites, with a singleton marker below each sprite and aligned to its center column.\n- The lower field contains only background and marker colors from the legend.\n\nRule:\n- Pair legend markers to legend sprites by left-to-right position.\n- Discard the legend and separator; keep the grid width and the rows below the separator.\n- In the lower field, replace every marker pixel by a filled square of the paired sprite color, centered at the marker location.\n\nKey insight: The top area is a positional color legend, and the actual output is the post-separator marker field expanded by that legend.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"22208ba4\" lines=\"12-27\">\n<description>\nMove the repeated boundary color's rectangles one block inward while leaving singleton boundary rectangles in place.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the most common color.\n- Foreground objects are solid monochrome rectangles touching a grid corner.\n- Exactly one foreground color appears as multiple separate 4-connected objects; other colors appear once.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the multiple objects of the repeated color from their original positions.\n- For each cleared rectangle, translate it away from the row and column border it touches by exactly its height and width.\n- Keep singleton-color objects unchanged; overlapping translated rectangles of the same color merge.\n\nKey insight:\n- Multiplicity selects the moving color, and each boundary rectangle's touched edges determine its inward diagonal translation.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"291dc1e1\" lines=\"7-22\">\n<description>\nReorder and stack rectangles by proximity to two colored edge lines.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Two edge lines (h + v) meet at a corner marked by a unique color.\n- \"Blue\" line is color 1 if present, else the longer line; other is \"red.\"\n- Solid rectangles in the interior.\n\nRule:\n- Sort rectangles by (distance to blue edge, distance to red edge).\n- If the blue edge is vertical, rotate each rectangle 90° CCW.\n- Stack top-to-bottom, centered horizontally.\n\nKey insight: Edge-line colors encode a coordinate system; proximity to each axis determines stacking order and rotation.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"984d8a3e\" lines=\"5-21\">\n<description>\nShift each row's dominant middle-color run left until its right edge aligns with the leftmost original right edge, moving displaced left-side pixels after the run.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has three colors.\n- The most common color forms one contiguous horizontal run in every row.\n- Pixels before those runs share one side color, and pixels after those runs share the other side color.\n\nRule:\n- Find the minimum right edge column among the middle-color runs.\n- In each row, keep the run width and the trailing right-side color count.\n- Place the middle-color run so its right edge is at that minimum column, unless the run is too wide, in which case start it at column 0.\n- Fill any remaining non-trailing cells with the left-side color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe varying row prefixes are movable padding; the stable feature is the leftmost right boundary of the middle-color shape.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3d588dc9\" lines=\"95-109\">\n<description>\nReplace the active black cutout's tail with background and mark the cutout side facing a colored source region.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant color is background, with black rectangle-plus-tail cutouts, one gray source region, and colored distractors.\n- Non-gray colored regions and single pixels are distractors/blockers, even when they are multi-pixel staircase shapes.\n\nRule:\n- Find each black cutout whose largest solid rectangle leaves exactly a two-pixel tail.\n- The active gray source region is visible only by horizontal rays through background from a cutout's left or right side.\n- Select the unique cutout side with the most same-source visible rows, erase that cutout's tail to background, and recolor the full selected vertical side pink (6).\n\nKey insight:\n- The colored regions do not move; their horizontal line-of-sight identifies which rectangular cutout is being opened and which side receives the pink mark.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"bd5af378\" lines=\"25-42\">\n<description>\nRewrite a corner L block into two nested L borders and a diagonal trace.\n\nInput structure\nA rectangular grid has exactly two colors: one color forms a one-cell-thick\nL on two adjacent outer edges, and the other color fills the remaining\nrectangle.\n\nRule\nNormalize the L to the top-left corner. Paint the outer top-left L with the\nfill color, the next inner L with the original border color, and the main\ndiagonal of the remaining inner rectangle with the fill color. All other\ncells become color 8, then the original orientation is restored.\n\nKey insight\nThe corner of the input L determines the orientation; after flipping to a\ncanonical top-left L, the output is the same nested-layer pattern for every\nexample.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"78332cb0\" lines=\"10-23\">\n<description>\nReorder 5×5 blocks into a connected strip by matching edge foreground pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background; sep = divider color (full row/column lines).\n- Several 5×5 sprite blocks in a grid, separated by sep lines.\n\nRule:\n- Two blocks \"connect\" when their facing edges share foreground pixels at the same offset (e.g., A's right edge ∩ B's left edge).\n- Chain all blocks in the orientation (horizontal or vertical) that admits a complete sequence.\n- Output is a 1×N strip of blocks in chain order, separated by sep lines.\n\nKey insight: Edge-contact overlap determines both block ordering and output orientation.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"45a5af55\" lines=\"5-18\">\n<description>\nBuild nested square frames from a stack of horizontal color stripes.\n\nInput structure:\n- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\n- Each stripe has uniform color and variable height (1-4 rows).\n\nRule:\n- Read stripes bottom to top.\n- Bottom stripe becomes the center solid square with side length = stripe height.\n- Each subsequent stripe wraps the current shape with a square frame of thickness = stripe height, in that stripe's color.\n\nKey insight: Stripe height doubles as both frame thickness and (for the innermost) center-square side length; output dimensions are fully determined by the stripe heights.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"c920a713\" lines=\"87-102\">\n<description>\nUntangle overlapping colored rectangular frames into concentric square frames ordered by their visible crossings.\n\nInput structure\n- The background contains several one-cell-thick axis-aligned rectangular frames, one color per frame.\n- Frames overlap, and the visible color at an overlap records a directed crossing from the hidden frame to the visible frame.\n- Each foreground color still has visible pixels on the perimeter of its full rectangular bounding box.\n\nRule\n- Infer each color's full rectangular frame from the bounding box of its visible pixels.\n- Add a directed edge A -> B when B is visible at a crossing of A and B's frame perimeters.\n- Find the unique path that visits every frame color once, then render those colors as one-pixel-thick concentric square frames from outside to inside.\n\nKey insight\n- The output is not a crop of the input; the crossing graph gives a single frame order, and that order is redrawn as nested rings.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"c803e39c\" lines=\"31-40\">\n<description>\nExpand the second mask into a block grid by stamping the first mask with the two payload colors.\n\nInput structure\n- A background grid has four panels separated by three full-height separator columns.\n- The first two panels contain same-size binary masks; the last two contain solid same-size color squares.\nRule\n- Use the second mask as an outer layout. For each foreground cell in that outer mask, place a tile equal to the first mask, coloring its foreground with the first solid-square color and its background with the second solid-square color; outer background cells become all second solid-square color.\nKey insight\n- The output is the Kronecker product of the two binary masks, with the two right-hand panel colors providing the palette.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2de01db2\" lines=\"28-41\">\n<description>\nInvert each row's native foreground color against the black background.\n\nInput structure\n- A black-background grid whose rows each have one native foreground color plus optional distractor colors.\n- The native row color is the most frequent non-bg color in that row; if tied, its run starts leftmost among tied colors.\n\nRule\n- For each row independently, turn pixels of the native row color into bg.\n- Turn every other pixel in that row, including bg and distractor colors, into the native row color.\n\nKey insight\n- Distractor colors are not preserved objects; they mark cells that participate in the binary complement of the row's native color.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"c9680e90\" lines=\"52-67\">\n<description>\nMove each mirrored bottom source pixel to the far end of its trail and redraw the top half as its reflection.\n\nInput structure\n- A solid non-background row separates equal-height top and bottom halves.\n- The top half has one marker color on the background.\n- In the bottom half, exactly one color has positions that mirror the top markers across the separator, and the other color forms trails touching those source pixels.\n\nRule\n- Identify the bottom source color by reflecting each bottom color into the top half and matching the top marker set.\n- For every bottom source pixel, follow its unique 4-connected trail of the other bottom color to the trail endpoint.\n- Clear the old top markers, bottom sources, and trails; place the source color at each endpoint and place the top marker color at the reflected endpoint.\n\nKey insight\n- The top half is only a mirror display of the bottom moving sources; the actual motion is encoded by the trail attached to each bottom source pixel.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8698868d\" lines=\"9-23\">\n<description>\nMatch sprites to frames by connected-hole count, then nest each sprite inside its frame.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = azure (8). Large hollow squares (frames) arranged in a grid; smaller filled squares (sprites) placed elsewhere.\n- Each frame and sprite has a distinct color. Sprites may contain holes (non-sprite-color pixels).\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1692361792/16/des.md\"","aggregated_output":"<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据边框缺口方向选择内部图案的旋转方式，再按图案中前景像素数确定嵌套复制层数。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（Black）。\n  - 网格中散布若干独立的正方形边框（由同一颜色绘制的一像素宽空心正方形），每个边框的四条边中恰好有一条边存在一个连续缺口（缺口长度至少2像素，缺口处为背景色）。\n  - 每个边框内部（不含边框本身）包含一个由另一种颜色绘制的小型图案（sprite），图案为非对称形状，占据边框内部区域的左上角对齐位置，其余内部像素为背景色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步（旋转选择）：根据缺口所在边确定旋转角度——缺口在上边：不旋转；缺口在右边：顺时针90度；缺口在下边：180度；缺口在左边：逆时针90度。将内部图案按该角度旋转。\n  - 第二步（嵌套复制）：数出旋转后图案中前景像素的个数 N（N 不超过 6）。以旋转后的图案为种子，向外嵌套 N 层同心方框，每层方框厚度为1像素，颜色交替使用边框颜色和图案颜色（最内层方框用边框颜色）。\n  - 输出网格仅保留所有嵌套结果，每个嵌套结构紧密裁切后按原输入中对应边框的相对空间顺序排列在新网格中，结构之间间隔1列或1行背景色。\n\n- `Key insight`：缺口方向不是装饰而是旋转指令，像素计数则控制嵌套深度——解题者需先发现方向-旋转映射，再发现计数-层数关系，两层规则缺一不可。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中散落的彩色路径片段按颜色配对，沿两段路径延伸方向用灰色走廊连通，再用连通走廊的转弯次数的奇偶性决定最终填充颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Azure。\n  - 网格中有若干条不同颜色的短路径片段（每种非背景、非灰色的颜色恰好出现两段，每段为3至5个像素的4-连通线段，方向为水平或垂直）。\n  - 每对同色路径片段之间存在一条唯一的由灰色（Grey）像素标记的管道走廊——走廊为宽度1像素的4-连通路径，两端分别与同色两段路径的端点相邻。\n  - 走廊可能包含若干个90度转弯。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每种颜色，找到其两段路径片段和连接它们的灰色走廊。\n  - 将灰色走廊像素重新着色为该对路径片段的颜色，使整条路径连通。\n  - 数出该走廊中90度转弯的次数 T：若 T 为奇数，将该连通路径的所有像素（含原始片段和走廊）替换为 Red；若 T 为偶数，替换为 Green。\n  - 原始路径片段的像素也一同替换颜色。\n\n- `Key insight`：灰色走廊是待着色的连接通道，但最终颜色不由原始路径颜色决定，而由走廊的几何形状（转弯奇偶性）决定——解题者需先识别配对机制，再发现转弯奇偶决定输出颜色的隐蔽规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：利用网格边缘的单行色带作为折叠轴颜色图例，将内部同色矩形沿匹配轴镜像翻折后叠合，重叠区域用特殊颜色标记。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格的上边缘有一行由若干段不同颜色组成的色带（每段覆盖连续若干列，颜色互不相同且非背景色）。左边缘有一列由若干段不同颜色组成的色带（每段覆盖连续若干行，颜色互不相同且非背景色）。上边缘色带和左边缘色带中恰好有若干颜色重复出现——每种重复颜色在上边缘出现一次、在左边缘出现一次。\n  - 网格内部（不含边缘色带行和列）包含若干个单色实心矩形，每个矩形的颜色恰好是某个在两条色带中都出现的颜色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个内部矩形，找到与其颜色匹配的上边缘色段和左边缘色段。\n  - 上边缘色段的水平中心列定义一条垂直折叠轴；左边缘色段的垂直中心行定义一条水平折叠轴。\n  - 将该矩形同时沿垂直轴左右镜像、沿水平轴上下镜像，产生最多四个副本（含原矩形）。\n  - 所有副本绘制在输出网格上（覆盖背景）；若任一像素被同一矩形的两个或更多副本覆盖，该像素着色为 Maroon（而非矩形原色）。不同颜色矩形的副本之间若重叠，后处理的覆盖先处理的。\n  - 处理顺序：按矩形面积从大到小；面积相同时按矩形左上角行号从小到大。\n  - 上边缘和左边缘色带在输出中保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：边缘色带不是装饰边框，而是为每个同色矩形同时指定两条折叠轴——解题者需先发现颜色匹配将色带与矩形关联，再发现色段中心即折叠轴，最后注意重叠区域的特殊标记色，形成三层推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在由分隔线划分的子区域中，每个区域内的箭头形状指向相邻区域，被指向的空区域需填充为箭头的颜色，多箭头竞争时由箭头面积仲裁。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格被 Grey 色的完整水平线和垂直线分割为若干矩形子区域（类似表格）。\n  - 部分子区域内包含一个由某种非背景、非灰色颜色绘制的箭头图案。箭头的绘制方式：一个实心的 3x3 正方形作为箭头主体，加上从主体某一边中心向外延伸的 2 像素长的单像素宽线段作为箭头尖端。尖端延伸方向即箭头指向方向（上、下、左、右四种之一）。\n  - 其余子区域为空（全部背景色）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个含箭头的子区域，确定箭头指向方向，找到沿该方向相邻的下一个子区域（跨过一条灰色分隔线）。\n  - 若目标子区域为空，则将目标子区域全部填充为箭头的颜色。\n  - 若目标子区域已含有箭头或已被其他箭头填充，则不做改变。\n  - 若一个空区域被多个箭头同时指向，比较这些箭头图案的前景像素总数（含主体和尖端），将该区域填充为像素数最多的箭头颜色；若像素数相同，则选择从上方或左方指来的箭头颜色（优先级：上 > 左 > 右 > 下）。\n  - 含箭头的区域本身保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：灰色网格线定义了区域拓扑，箭头的尖端方向是传播指令而非运动路径——解题者需先识别箭头形状与朝向的编码方式，再理解指向相邻区域并填色的传播规则，最后在多箭头竞争时发现面积优先的仲裁机制。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：网格中每个彩色环形框内的小图案需被投影到环形框缺口对面的墙壁外侧，投影颜色由框色决定而非图案色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中包含若干个由不同颜色绘制的一像素宽正方形空心框（环形框），每个框的四条边中恰好一条边上有一个连续缺口（缺口处为背景色），缺口宽度为2或3像素。\n  - 每个环形框内部中央有一个由另一种颜色（与框色不同）绘制的小型连通图案，图案的紧密包围盒不超过 4x4。\n  - 环形框外部全为背景。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个环形框，确定缺口所在边及其对面边（即投影墙）。\n  - 将内部图案从框内移除（填为背景色），然后将图案投射到投影墙外侧：图案紧贴投影墙外表面放置，水平或垂直方向居中对齐于框的中轴线。\n  - 投影时图案需沿缺口到投影墙的方向做镜像翻转（左右缺口时做水平翻转，上下缺口时做垂直翻转）。\n  - 投影图案的颜色变为环形框的颜色（而非原图案颜色）。\n  - 环形框本身（含缺口）保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：缺口不是出口而是光源方向——图案被投影到缺口的对面而非从缺口射出，且投影颜色由框色决定而非图案色。解题者需先发现缺口与投影方向的反直觉关系，再发现颜色替换规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据分隔符两侧图案的逐像素差异，在第三面板中用红绿双色分别标记仅属于左侧和仅属于右侧的差异像素。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格被两条完整的垂直 Grey 线分为三个等宽面板（左、中、右）。\n  - 左面板和中面板各包含一个由同一种颜色（如 Blue）绘制的图案，两个图案整体形状相似但存在若干像素位置差异（即左面板有而中面板没有的前景像素，以及中面板有而左面板没有的前景像素）。\n  - 右面板初始为全背景色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 逐像素比较左面板与中面板在相同相对位置上的内容。\n  - 找出所有仅在左面板出现的前景像素位置集合 A，以及仅在中面板出现的前景像素位置集合 B。\n  - 将集合 A 的像素用 Red 绘制在右面板的对应相对位置上。\n  - 将集合 B 的像素用 Green 绘制在右面板的对应相对位置上。\n  - 两个图案中相同位置的共有前景像素不出现在右面板中。\n\n- `Key insight`：左中两个面板看起来像找不同游戏，但输出不是简单标记差异位置，而是将差异像素按来源方向分色绘制到第三面板——解题者需先逐像素对比发现差异，再理解红绿分色编码了差异的方向性，即哪一侧多出来的像素对应哪种颜色。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：网格中的彩色种子像素沿灰色引导轨道生长为线段，生长长度由种子在轨道上的排列位次决定，最终轨道自身被擦除。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有若干条灰色（Grey）直线轨道，每条轨道为水平或垂直的连续灰色像素段，长度至少为5。\n  - 每条轨道上散布着若干个不同颜色的单个种子像素（颜色非黑非灰），种子像素覆盖在轨道上（即种子所在位置的底层为灰色轨道的一部分）。\n  - 每条轨道上的种子颜色互不相同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每条轨道，按照种子在轨道上的排列顺序（水平轨道从左到右，垂直轨道从上到下）给种子编号 1、2、3，依此类推。\n  - 每个编号为 k 的种子，沿垂直于轨道的方向（水平轨道的种子向上生长，垂直轨道的种子向左生长）绘制一条长度为 k 像素的线段（不含种子自身位置），颜色为种子的颜色。\n  - 绘制完成后，将所有灰色轨道像素（未被种子覆盖的部分）擦除为背景色。种子自身像素保留。\n\n- `Key insight`：轨道是临时的结构支架——它既定义了生长方向（垂直于轨道），又通过种子在轨道上的排列位次隐式编码了每颗种子的生长长度。解题者需先发现位置顺序与长度的对应关系，再注意轨道在输出中消失。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将输入网格中的多个不规则形状按照它们与网格外边界接触的边数进行分组，同组形状提取后按数量排序水平拼接为条带，不同条带从上到下按组内形状数排列。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Azure。\n  - 网格中散布若干个单色4-连通不规则形状（每个形状颜色可能相同也可能不同），形状之间互不相邻。\n  - 每个形状的紧密包围盒不超过 5x5。\n  - 部分形状的像素接触网格的一条外边界（即像素位于第0行、最后一行、第0列或最后一列），部分形状接触两条外边界（位于角落附近，像素同时出现在相邻的两条边界上），部分形状完全不接触任何边界（位于内部）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 按每个形状接触网格外边界的边数（0条、1条、2条）将形状分为三组。这里\"接触边数\"指的是形状的像素实际触及了几条不同的网格边界线（上、下、左、右各算一条）。\n  - 对每组内的形状，按其在原网格中的位置从左到右（按包围盒左上角列号）、从上到下（列号相同时按行号）排序，然后将每个形状的紧密包围盒提取出来，沿水平方向依次紧密拼接（相邻形状间隔1列背景色），形成该组的输出条带。\n  - 输出网格中，各条带从上到下排列（相邻条带间隔1行背景色），排列顺序按每组包含的形状数量从多到少；若数量相同，接触边数多的组排在上方。\n\n- `Key insight`：形状的颜色和具体轮廓都不是分组依据——分组的关键是每个形状与网格边界的空间关系（接触几条边），这是一个需要逐个形状检查其边界位置的非显然分类标准。解题者需先发现分组规律，再理解条带的排序和拼接规则。\n</new_puzzle>","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
