{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/16/codegen_prompts/4.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1692361792/16`\n- 题号：`4`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/16/4.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"4\">\n- `description`：在由分隔线划分的子区域中，每个区域内的箭头形状指向相邻区域，被指向的空区域需填充为箭头的颜色，多箭头竞争时由箭头面积仲裁。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格被 Grey 色的完整水平线和垂直线分割为若干矩形子区域（类似表格）。\n  - 部分子区域内包含一个由某种非背景、非灰色颜色绘制的箭头图案。箭头的绘制方式：一个实心的 3x3 正方形作为箭头主体，加上从主体某一边中心向外延伸的 2 像素长的单像素宽线段作为箭头尖端。尖端延伸方向即箭头指向方向（上、下、左、右四种之一）。\n  - 其余子区域为空（全部背景色）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个含箭头的子区域，确定箭头指向方向，找到沿该方向相邻的下一个子区域（跨过一条灰色分隔线）。\n  - 若目标子区域为空，则将目标子区域全部填充为箭头的颜色。\n  - 若目标子区域已含有箭头或已被其他箭头填充，则不做改变。\n  - 若一个空区域被多个箭头同时指向，比较这些箭头图案的前景像素总数（含主体和尖端），将该区域填充为像素数最多的箭头颜色；若像素数相同，则选择从上方或左方指来的箭头颜色（优先级：上 > 左 > 右 > 下）。\n  - 含箭头的区域本身保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：灰色网格线定义了区域拓扑，箭头的尖端方向是传播指令而非运动路径——解题者需先识别箭头形状与朝向的编码方式，再理解指向相邻区域并填色的传播规则，最后在多箭头竞争时发现面积优先的仲裁机制。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/332f06d7, eval/9385bd28, train/a416fc5b, train/538b439f, eval/8f3a5a89, train/9f669b64, train/753ea09b, eval/0934a4d8\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"332f06d7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3905\nmechanism=0.4692\nlexical=0.0141\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:marker, object:path, object:square, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, output:same_size, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/332f06d7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\n- Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\n\nRule:\n- The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\n- It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\n- If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\n- The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\n\nKey insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"black square\",\n  \"path\": \"blue pixels \\\"water channel\\\" that is wide enough to pass through until \\\"stuck\\\" because of too narrow\",\n  \"dst\": \"reach same sized red square or \\\"get stuck\\\" on the way where the blue path is too narrow\",\n  \"transform\": \"cover the red square if reaching it\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"9385bd28\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3408\nmechanism=0.4477\nlexical=0.0107\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:counter, object:axis, object:marker, object:path, object:rectangle, object:sprite, object:square, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/9385bd28.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/9385bd28.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill rectangles between diagonal marker pairs using a color legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg grid with a vertical legend at the bottom-left: each row is a (marker_color, fill_color) pair.\n- Scattered L-shaped corner markers of each marker color define opposite corners of axis-aligned rectangles.\n- Some markers are solid 2×2 blocks instead of corner pairs.\n\nRule:\n- Read legend bottom-to-top; for each entry find all pixels of that marker color.\n- Determine which two bbox corners carry L-shaped anchors — the *other* diagonal defines the fill region.\n- Fill the diamond (all shortest-path cells between those two corners) with the legend's fill color.\n- Solid 2×2 marker blocks are simply recolored to the fill color.\n- Later legend entries are protected from earlier fills.\n\nKey insight: The L-shaped anchors sit on the marker diagonal; the fill goes on the opposite diagonal of the bounding box.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color legend at bottom-left to find diagonal marker pairs of matching color, then fill the rectangle between them with the adjacent legend color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"diagonal pixel pair s with same color forming opposite corners of a rectangle (upper corner pixel)\",\n  \"dst\": \"diagonal pixel pair d with same color forming opposite corners of a rectangle (lower corner pixel)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.color == d.color && s and d are diagonally opposite\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill rectangle bounded by s and d with color from legend where legend.left == s.color gives fill_color = legend.right\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend is vertical stack of color pairs at bottom-left, each pair (left-right only) has marker color on left and fill color on right\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify legend as vertically stacked color pairs at bottom-left corner; Step 2: process legend entries from bottom to top; Step 3: for each legend entry (marker_color on left, fill_color on right), find all diagonal pairs of marker_color pixels; Step 4: fill rectangle between each diagonal pair with fill_color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-legend\",\n    \"diagonal-markers\",\n    \"rectangle-fill\",\n    \"ordered-processing\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"sometimes as 2x2 squares which count as two diagonal triangles; processing order matters for overlapping regions\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a416fc5b\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2980\nmechanism=0.4042\nlexical=0.0161\ncode_feature=0.1667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:axis, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:sprite, object:square, operation:count, relation:adjacent, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/a416fc5b.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/a416fc5b.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nAdd the two missing colored arms of a centered diamond-sprite motif, or clear a completed motif to a blank square.\n\nInput structure\nAn 11x11 board has orange background and pink separator bars forming nine 3x3 cells. Occupied cells contain a four-pixel diamond sprite; the center cell and one neighboring cell are red, and a completed board may also contain one grey and one teal sprite.\n\nRule\nWith only the two red sprites present, preserve the board and add grey and teal diamond sprites 135 degrees clockwise and counterclockwise from the non-center red arm. If those expected grey and teal sprites are already present, output an all-background square whose side length is the total number of sprite pixels.\n\nKey insight\nThe non-center red sprite is an eight-neighbor direction from the center; the other two colored arms are fixed rotations of that direction.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"3x3 cell board with a red center diamond sprite and one red neighboring diamond sprite\",\n  \"dst\": \"the two rotated arm cells of the centered motif\",\n  \"transform\": \"add a grey sprite 135 degrees clockwise and a teal sprite 135 degrees counterclockwise from the red arm around the center; if both are already present, erase to an all-background 16x16 square\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"same for the adding step; completed motif becomes 16x16\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"538b439f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3048\nmechanism=0.3567\nlexical=0.0115\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:path, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, output:same_size, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/538b439f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/538b439f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReflect the solid rectangular source objects across the full separator line and color the gap with the separator color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one full-width or full-height one-pixel\n  separator line in a non-background color.\n- One other foreground color forms solid rectangular objects, all strictly on the same side of that separator.\n- Remaining non-background pixels are scattered distractors.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input grid shape and unchanged pixels outside each affected corridor.\n- Mirror each source object across the separator line.\n- For every source object, recolor the rectangular strip between the\n  original object and its reflection to the separator color, then paint the\n  reflected object in the source color.\n\nKey insight:\n- The full straight line is a mirror axis; the real objects are identified\n  structurally as the only solid rectangles confined to one side, while\n  scattered pixels are noise that may be overwritten inside the corridor.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"solid rectangular foreground objects all on one side of the full separator row/column\",\n  \"dst\": \"their mirror positions across the separator line\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy each source object by reflection; recolor the rectangular strip between each source object and its mirror to the separator color, overwriting background or distractor pixels inside that strip\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8f3a5a89\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3052\nmechanism=0.3447\nlexical=0.0114\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:closed_region, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:path, object:sprite, operation:flood_fill, relation:adjacent\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8f3a5a89.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPaint an inner border around the region reachable from a corner marker pixel.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; wall color (blue) forms barriers dividing the grid.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
